---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
---

<Site
	title="Resume · Steven Vanden Heuvel"
	description="Product designer with design systems depth who builds the tooling a design team needs. Most recently Principal Designer at PayPal on contract, after 18 years at MTG Media Group."
	image="/og/resume.png"
>
	<article class="rs">
		<header class="rs-head">
			<p class="sdc-eyebrow">Resume</p>
			<h1 class="rs-name sdc-display">Steven Vanden Heuvel</h1>
			<p class="rs-role">Staff Product Designer · Design Systems &amp; AI Tooling</p>
			<p class="rs-loc">Aurora, IL · Chicago area · Open to remote</p>
			<ul class="rs-contact">
				<li class="print-only">630.862.6534</li>
				<li><a class="sdc-js-email" data-eml="73746576656e4073746576656e64657369676e636f2e636f6d" href="#">steven [at] stevendesignco [dot] com</a></li>
				<li><a href="https://www.stevendesignco.com">stevendesignco.com</a></li>
				<li><a href="https://linkedin.com/in/stevendesignco" target="_blank" rel="noopener">linkedin.com/in/stevendesignco<span class="sdc-u-sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a></li>
				<li><a href="https://github.com/vandy1690" target="_blank" rel="noopener">github.com/vandy1690<span class="sdc-u-sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a></li>
			</ul>
			<a class="sdc-btn sdc-btn--primary rs-pdf" href="/resume.pdf" download>Download PDF</a>
		</header>

		<section class="rs-sec">
			<h2 class="sdc-eyebrow">Summary</h2>
			<p class="rs-summary">Product designer who takes a flow from problem framing through interaction and visual design to handoff, and builds the tooling that makes the next one faster. Most recently Principal Designer at PayPal on contract, where a self-initiated Figma plugin cut merchant flow setup from most of a day to 10 to 15 minutes. Spent 18 years at MTG Media Group designing the websites for 7 publication brands, ending as VP and Creative Director, and won four Jesse H. Neal Awards, including Best Website. 27 years of bringing new technique into industries early: responsive design in B2B publishing before it was standard, then Atomic Design and component-based design systems, Figma, Storybook, and Claude Code and Cursor now.</p>
		</section>

		<section class="rs-sec">
			<h2 class="sdc-eyebrow">Experience</h2>
			<div class="rs-jobs">
				<div class="rs-job">
					<h3 class="rs-job__role">Product Designer and Founder</h3>
					<p class="rs-job__org">Steven Design Co (Steven Design Services LLC)</p>
					<p class="rs-job__meta">Remote, IL · May 2018 to present · Self-employed</p>
					<ul class="rs-points">
						<li>Built the Steven Design Co design system in Figma and Storybook, WCAG tested and kept in step both ways with AI.</li>
						<li>Designed and built SDC Claude Code Router, which picks the Claude model for each prompt (github.com/vandy1690).</li>
						<li>Building the brand identity and website for The Artistic Eye, a gallery and optical shop.</li>
					</ul>
				</div>

				<div class="rs-job">
					<h3 class="rs-job__role">Principal Designer, Merchant Enablement Checkout</h3>
					<p class="rs-job__org">PayPal · Contract</p>
					<p class="rs-job__meta">Remote, IL · December 2025 to August 2026</p>
					<ul class="rs-points">
						<li>On my own initiative, built a Figma plugin that cut merchant flow setup from most of a day to 10 to 15 minutes across PayPal's top 38 merchants. PMs and designers had been using different vocabulary for the same flow elements, so the plugin made the flow skeleton a shared reference. Adopted and in use, published to the internal GitHub with video tutorials, and handed off to another designer to broaden.</li>
						<li>Produced 20+ complete merchant proposal packages for PayPal's top 100 global brands on weekly sprints. The program's product manager credited the team with moving top accounts to integration or launch.</li>
						<li>Designed generic one-click checkout flows for grocery, retail, restaurant, and subscription merchants, mostly mobile, from product selection through payment confirmation, so one pattern set held across categories.</li>
						<li>Built the Figma board that traced the checkout dead end, where a customer has no working card, back to the earlier points where they could have fixed it. Structured it with Claude Code from a director's diagram and gathered screens from teams across the company. The work reached senior leadership and became the team's template for mapping the next flows.</li>
					</ul>
				</div>

				<div class="rs-job">
					<h3 class="rs-job__role">VP / Creative Director (Design Systems &amp; Web)</h3>
					<p class="rs-job__org">MTG Media Group</p>
					<p class="rs-job__meta">Chicago, IL and remote · October 2007 to May 2025 · VP / Creative Director from January 2019, promoted from Senior Art Director / Senior Interface Designer</p>
					<ul class="rs-points">
						<li>Led a 6-person creative team across 7 publication brands and 6 responsive web products, building and owning the design system behind each of the 6 sites.</li>
						<li>Initiated the brand-site rebuilds and introduced mobile-first responsive design, Figma, and Atomic Design through Pattern Lab, and began the team's move to Storybook.js.</li>
						<li>Wrote one set of contribution and review rules for the site design systems, adopted by engineers outside the design team.</li>
						<li>Did all the Drupal theming for Plate and Alt-Meat directly in the code, plus some block creation and work in nodes, modules and menus: SCSS, PHP, YAML and edits to the JavaScript. Later themed the headless rebuild in Tailwind.</li>
						<li>Interviewed stakeholders across editorial, sales, IT, and ownership before the Plate and Hotels rebuilds, ran task-based usability tests on Plate through UserTesting.com, and followed sessions and heatmaps in Google Analytics and Lucky Orange. When testers kept flagging registration as long and intrusive, redesigned the flow with the publisher to ask less up front and collect data over time; that flow became the base for Alt-Meat registration.</li>
						<li>Plate: won the 2017 Jesse H. Neal Award (the B2B equivalent of the Pulitzer Prize) for Best Website. Rebuilt as a responsive, mobile-first product serving 42,000 print and digital subscribers with 56,000 average monthly pageviews.</li>
						<li>Project Blackbird: built an interactive oral history with a dozen video interviews, original photography, and illustrations. Won the Jesse H. Neal Award for Best Profile and was a Grand Neal finalist.</li>
						<li>Alt-Meat: launched a brand, magazine, and website from zero in under 8 weeks as the first major B2B publication in alternative protein, and designed its identity from scratch.</li>
					</ul>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="rs-sec">
			<h2 class="sdc-eyebrow">Skills</h2>
			<ul class="rs-skills">
				<li>Product Design</li>
				<li>UX Design</li>
				<li>UI Design</li>
				<li>Interaction Design</li>
				<li>Visual Design</li>
				<li>Payments and Checkout</li>
				<li>Financial Products</li>
				<li>Internal Tools and Admin UX</li>
				<li>Design Systems</li>
				<li>Design Tokens</li>
				<li>Atomic Design</li>
				<li>Storybook</li>
				<li>Responsive Web</li>
				<li>Prototyping</li>
				<li>Wireframing</li>
				<li>Usability Testing</li>
				<li>Accessibility (WCAG)</li>
				<li>Stakeholder Workshops</li>
				<li>Brand Identity</li>
				<li>Editorial and Print Design</li>
				<li>Figma</li>
				<li>Figma Plugin Development</li>
				<li>HTML</li>
				<li>CSS</li>
				<li>Sass</li>
				<li>Drupal Theming</li>
				<li>WordPress</li>
				<li>Reading and Debugging JavaScript, Node.js and React</li>
				<li>AI Assisted Development (Claude Code, Cursor, MCP)</li>
				<li>Illustrator</li>
				<li>Photoshop</li>
				<li>InDesign</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<section class="rs-sec">
			<h2 class="sdc-eyebrow">Recognition</h2>
			<ul class="rs-recognition">
				<li>4 Jesse H. Neal Awards</li>
				<li>6 Neal Finalists</li>
				<li>1 Grand Neal Finalist (top 4 nationally)</li>
				<li>Folio OZZIE Honorable Mention</li>
				<li>Multiple ASBPE Awards</li>
				<li>Northwestern Medill Guest Speaker</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<section class="rs-sec">
			<h2 class="sdc-eyebrow">Education</h2>
			<p class="rs-education">University of Wisconsin-Whitewater, B.A. in Art with emphasis in Graphic Design and Marketing</p>
			<p class="rs-education">AI &amp; Design Systems certificate, Brad Frost Web, 2026</p>
		</section>
	</article>
</Site>

<style>
	.rs { max-width: var(--sdc-max-narrow); margin: 0 auto; padding: var(--sdc-space-3xl) var(--sdc-gutter) var(--sdc-space-4xl); }

	/* Header */
	.rs-head .sdc-eyebrow { margin-bottom: var(--sdc-space-sm); }
	.rs-name { font-size: clamp(40px, 6vw, 72px); letter-spacing: -0.02em; margin: 0 0 var(--sdc-space-md); }
	.rs-role { font-size: clamp(20px, 2vw, 26px); font-weight: 600; color: var(--sdc-text); margin: 0 0 var(--sdc-space-sm); letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
	.rs-loc { color: var(--sdc-text-mute); font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 var(--sdc-space-md); }
	.rs-contact { list-style: none; margin: 0 0 var(--sdc-space-lg); padding: 0; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px var(--sdc-space-md); font-size: 15px; font-weight: 500; }
	/* Same 24px minimum as the home page contact list. It sat at 19. Reset in
	   print below, where the type is 9.5px and target size does not apply. */
	.rs-contact a { color: var(--sdc-text); text-decoration: underline; text-decoration-thickness: 1px; text-underline-offset: 3px; transition: color 0.14s ease; padding-block: 3px; }
	.rs-contact a:hover { color: var(--sdc-accent); }
	.rs-pdf { margin-top: var(--sdc-space-xs); }

	/* Sections, divided by rules */
	.rs-sec { margin-top: var(--sdc-space-2xl); padding-top: var(--sdc-space-2xl); border-top: 1px solid var(--sdc-rule); }
	.rs-sec > .sdc-eyebrow { margin-bottom: var(--sdc-space-md); }

	/* Summary: eyebrow + this lead read as the headline */
	.rs-summary { font-size: clamp(22px, 2.4vw, 30px); font-weight: 600; color: var(--sdc-text); line-height: 1.3; letter-spacing: -0.015em; margin: 0; max-width: 40ch; }

	/* Experience */
	.rs-jobs { display: grid; gap: var(--sdc-space-2xl); }
	.rs-job__role { font-size: clamp(20px, 2.2vw, 24px); font-weight: 700; color: var(--sdc-text); line-height: 1.2; letter-spacing: -0.015em; margin: 0 0 var(--sdc-space-xs); }
	.rs-job__org { color: var(--sdc-text); font-size: 16px; font-weight: 600; margin: 0; }
	.rs-job__meta { color: var(--sdc-text-mute); font-size: 13px; letter-spacing: 0.02em; margin: var(--sdc-space-xs) 0 0; }
	.rs-points { list-style: none; margin: var(--sdc-space-md) 0 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: var(--sdc-space-sm); }
	.rs-points li { position: relative; padding-left: var(--sdc-space-md); color: var(--sdc-text-mute); font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.6; }
	.rs-points li::before { content: ""; position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0.62em; width: 6px; height: 6px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--sdc-accent); }

	/* Skills: pills, matching the homepage capability tags */
	.rs-skills { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 10px; }
	.rs-skills li { padding: 10px 16px; border: 1px solid var(--sdc-rule); border-radius: 999px; font-size: 14px; color: var(--sdc-text); font-weight: 500; }

	/* Recognition: flowing list with accent dot separators */
	.rs-recognition { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px 0; font-size: 16px; color: var(--sdc-text); }
	.rs-recognition li { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; }
	.rs-recognition li:not(:last-child)::after { content: "·"; color: var(--sdc-accent); margin: 0 12px; font-weight: 700; }

	/* Education */
	.rs-education { margin: 0; font-size: 16px; color: var(--sdc-text); }

	@media (max-width: 700px) {
		.rs { padding-top: var(--sdc-space-2xl); }
		.rs-recognition { display: grid; gap: var(--sdc-space-xs); }
		.rs-recognition li:not(:last-child)::after { content: none; }
	}

	/* Print: the downloadable PDF is generated from this page, so the phone number
	   rides along in print only and the page chrome drops out. */
	.print-only { display: none; }
	@media print {
		.print-only { display: list-item; }
		.rs { padding: 0 !important; max-width: none; }
		.rs-pdf { display: none !important; }
		.rs-sec, .rs-job { break-inside: avoid; }
		.rs-head .sdc-eyebrow { display: none; }
		.rs-name { font-size: 26px !important; margin: 0 0 2px !important; }
		.rs-role { font-size: 13px !important; margin: 0 0 2px !important; }
		.rs-loc { font-size: 9.5px !important; margin: 0 0 3px !important; color: #444 !important; }
		.rs-contact { font-size: 9.5px !important; gap: 1px 12px !important; margin: 0 !important; }
		.rs-contact a { text-decoration: none !important; padding-block: 0 !important; }
		.rs-sec { margin-top: 10px !important; padding-top: 8px !important; }
		.rs-sec > .sdc-eyebrow { font-size: 8px !important; letter-spacing: 0.14em !important; margin-bottom: 5px !important; }
		.rs-summary { font-size: 10px !important; font-weight: 500 !important; line-height: 1.4 !important; letter-spacing: 0 !important; max-width: none !important; }
		.rs-jobs { gap: 10px !important; }
		.rs-job__role { font-size: 12px !important; margin-bottom: 1px !important; }
		.rs-job__org { font-size: 10px !important; }
		.rs-job__meta { font-size: 9px !important; margin-top: 1px !important; color: #444 !important; }
		.rs-points { margin-top: 5px !important; gap: 3px !important; }
		.rs-points li { font-size: 9.5px !important; line-height: 1.38 !important; padding-left: 11px !important; color: #333 !important; }
		.rs-points li::before { width: 3px; height: 3px; top: 0.5em; background: #666 !important; }
		.rs-skills { gap: 4px !important; }
		.rs-skills li { padding: 2px 7px !important; font-size: 8.5px !important; border-radius: 4px !important; }
		.rs-recognition { font-size: 9.5px !important; }
		.rs-recognition li:not(:last-child)::after { margin: 0 6px !important; }
		.rs-education { font-size: 9.5px !important; }
	}
</style>
